186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 123 0 R
/T (A late order loses two stars.)
/E (A late order loses two stars.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (This is the finding that changed our view of the problem. We put every order in a group, from the ones that arrived very early to the ones that arrived very late, and then we looked at the score the customer gave afterwards.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (When the parcel arrives on time, the average score is 4.29. When it arrives late, the average falls to 2.27. That is a drop of 2.02 points on a scale of five, and it happens with the same products, the same sellers and the same prices. The only thing that changed is the date. Each group in the chart also carries a confidence interval, so we know the fall is a pattern and not the noise of a few angry customers.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (For the business this is the real price of a broken promise. A score near two stars pushes the seller down in the search results, it makes the next customer doubt, and it often ends in a support ticket. One delivery that misses the date is enough to turn a satisfied customer into a public complaint.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 123 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/A [447 0 R 0]
/Alt (04_box_review_by_delay_ci.png)
/K [5]
>>
endobj
191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 123 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/A [448 0 R 0]
/K [6]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 124 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/A [449 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 124 0 R
/T (The money at risk.)
/E (The money at risk.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (A bad review hurts, but it is hard to defend a budget with stars alone. So we asked a second question: how much money travels inside the orders that arrive late?)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The goods inside those orders are worth R$ 985,618.47, which is 7.5% of the value we can check in the period. That money is not lost, because the customer already paid for it. It is money that sits with people who have a good reason to complain, to ask for help, to return the parcel or to buy somewhere else next time. It is the part of the revenue that the company puts at risk every time it misses a date.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The screen on the left is the page of our dashboard where those numbers live together. A manager can filter by date, region, product family or payment type, and the whole page answers at once. That way the discussion stops being about opinions and starts being about which part of the business is exposed this month. The same filters are the ones we would use to check whether an action worked later, so this page is also our follow up tool.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 124 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/A [450 0 R 0]
/Alt (01_overview.png)
/K [5]
>>
endobj
